# File browser session (make test): keyboard and mouse, pictures at the marked times.
# The browser starts by itself (INIT runs "SH files").
1500 {down}{down}{down}{down}
# shot 8 at 1.9 s: four single steps within the page: only "many" is inverse
+500 \n
# /many: 250 entries
+3000 {pgdn}{pgdn}
+1000 is
# shot 1 at 7.0 s: "Isn't it_odd + strange!.xex" selected on page 2
+2000 {end}
+1000 {home}
# the wheel scrolls (down 2 steps = 6 lines), a double click on the line under the
# pointer (y 180 = list row 14) runs it: the Atari, then F12 back
+1000 M 0:0:-2:0
+500 M 0:0:0:1
+100 M 0:0:0:0
+100 M 0:0:0:1
+100 M 0:0:0:0
+2000 {F12}
# shot 2 at 14.0 s: back in /many, the status line shows the executable
+2000 \b
# back in /, "many" selected again; type-ahead finds the rest
+1500 docs
+1500 \n
+1500 read
+1000 \n
# the pager: "Read me first.txt", its first page
# shot 3 at 22.0 s
+3000 q
+1000 \b
+1500 carts
+1000 \n
+1500 don
+1000 \n
+2000 {F12}
# Donkey Kong (a cartridge) ran: the status line has only the cartridge
# shot 4 at 32.5 s
+2000 \b
+1500 disks
+1000 \n
+1500 cav
+1000 \n
+2000 {F12}
# Caverns of Mars (a disk) ran: the cartridge is ejected, D1: has the disk
# shot 5 at 41.5 s
+2500 {esc}
# shot 6 at 44.0 s: the shell
# the shell: a paged ls of the 250-entry folder
+1500 cd many\n
+1500 ls\n
# shot 7 at 47.5 s: the first page and the "more" prompt
+2500 q
